<title>USA: Morton International to buy Singapore plant.</title>
<headline>Morton International to buy Singapore plant.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morton International Inc said Wednesday it will buy a manufacturing plant in Singapore from a subsidiary of Zeneca Group Plc of London for an undisclosed price.</p>
<p>Morton said it plans to make water-based polymers and packaging adhesives for flexible food packages. The sale, expected to be completed in May, includes the manufacturing facility, a warehouse and offices, Morton said.</p>
<p>Morton is a manufacturer of specialty chemicals, automotive restraint systems and salt.</p>
<p>Its shares were off 1/4 Wednesday at 43.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
